Z||000000||TRL46202||01-12-2000||10:09 AM||||I have an 87GT (155,000 +) v6 Auto. doesn't burn oil or smoke and runs great! The oil pressure seems good at startup (80) but as I drive (engine warms up 180) the pressure drops slow to (40-50) and stays that way. At idle (stopped, still in gear)it's just at (10-15), but when putting into park it goes up to 20. Does this mean I need a new oil pump or oil sensing unit? or is this pressure good?<P>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||chris6878||01-12-2000||11:50 AM||||mine does about the same... and the engine is newly rebuilt. I am using Penzoil 5W30 oil...    I think mine is related to my idling.. becuase its idling to low in park after it warms up....  it sits around 500 rpms after warming up while in park...         I think the normal idle should be 900 or 1000 rpms.  Correct me if i am wrong...       ||||reg||1
Z||000002||TRL46202||01-12-2000||11:53 AM||||Mine idles at about 8-900, but still reads 10-15 on the oil gage. You think that's ok? did you indstall a high volume oil pump, if so what kind?<P>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000003||sluppy123||01-12-2000||12:49 PM||||I have a 87' GT auto with a fresh engine (4k miles) and a high volume Sealed Power oil pump. My oil pressure is the same as you describe. <P>BTW I'm running full synthetic Mobil 1 10W-30<P>-Brian||||reg||1
Z||000004||TRL46202||01-12-2000||12:51 PM||||Thanks, I'll keep watching it......||||reg||1
Z||000005||Eric||01-12-2000||03:10 PM||||With my new engine, I installed a mechanical oil pressure gauge.  It confirmed that my old gauge wasn't reading funny.  Believe it or not, my oil pressure gets down to 5-8 psi at idle when warm with 10W40 oil and a high volume oil pump, but when I step on the accelerator, the pressure goes up with the revs.||||reg||1
Z||000006||GT Bastard||01-12-2000||05:54 PM||||I have the same car, and the same thing happens to me.  As long as the pressure increases with the RPM's, you're ok.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cooter||01-12-2000||08:50 PM||||The 2.8 in grandpaw's S10 holds between 0 and 1 psi of oil pressure idling and between 10 and 15 at highway speeds. The pressure light doesn't go off until about 1500 rpms! A mechanical gauge was added to check for sure, the engine just does not have any oil pressure. He drives it everyday and never had any problems with it.||||reg||1
Z||000008||2birds||01-12-2000||10:30 PM||||Mine runs around 60# at cold startup, 1400 rpm idle, and when warmed up idling at 900-1000, it runs around 35#, but it runs 40-45# just off idle.  I have always run 10w-40 Havoline year round, except for when I was living up north.  164,000 miles, V-6 5-speed.  I don't use any oil between changes, either.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Phaeton||01-13-2000||03:21 AM||||I use mobile 0w-30 in winter and syntec 5w-50 in the summer, both go down to twenty pounds at idle and hold fortyfive anywhere above 2000 rpm. V6.<p>[This message has been edited by Phaeton (edited 01-13-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||RossT||01-13-2000||03:38 AM||||My 88gt, seven hundred original miles, does about the same, maybee a little bit higher on<BR>the low end when fully warmed. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||86SE||01-14-2000||10:45 PM||||My 86 SE auto V-6, at idle speeds 800-2000, the guage reads 75-80 psi, if I give it a quick rev it drops quick to 45-50 psi, but a normal 55-70 MPH driving speeds its at around 80 psi....||||reg||1
Z||000012||Old Lar||01-15-2000||11:28 AM||||My '87 GT oil pressure runs high when cold 70-80 psi then settles down 50-60 when running.  I am also on my 3rd oil pressure sending unit.  I replace when the oil pressure went off scale.<P>The guages are not too accurate.<P>My '88 GT runs at 50-60 all the time.  Pontiac change the design for oil pressure sending unit for '88. Still not the best in the world, or so I have been told.||||reg||1
